{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":116821,"duration_api_ms":197241,"num_turns":5,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f95c7282-b5ea-4d36-becb-02b65a45d04b","total_cost_usd":0.55666925,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27393,"cache_read_input_tokens":80245,"output_tokens":2519,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27393,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":173,"outputTokens":9952,"cacheReadInputTokens":1141750,"cacheCreationInputTokens":94590,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2823455,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2519,"cacheReadInputTokens":80245,"cacheCreationInputTokens":27393,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.27432375,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All three amendments are verified against the source code and identify real correctness issues. The carbonate profile fixture produces invalid pH at the validation boundary, the unconditional runtime molt-timer fallback defeats the schema-guarded migration, and the chloride protection test is confounded by multiple chemistry changes from the replacement water with no control run.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-27e2dd70","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: salt_treatment_source_profile() uses WaterState::default_for_volume_l(1.0) giving DIC=20.0 mg C/L and alkalinity=1.5 meq/L. The carbonate solver derives pH=8.5 from these values, and validate_source_water_carbonate_profile() at chemistry.rs:477 rejects pH >= CARBONATE_PH_MAX (8.5) unless the status is ZeroDicBufferedLimit — which won't trigger with DIC=20.0. The fixture is genuinely invalid and needs adjustment to produce a pH strictly below 8.5."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-8281d091","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: shrimp.rs lines 508-523 contain an unconditional fallback that copies inter_molt_timer_days into per-stage timers whenever all three are zero. save.rs lines 960-976 contain identical logic but guarded by source_schema_version < PER_STAGE_MOLT_TIMER_SCHEMA_VERSION (13). Because the runtime fallback runs every molt_cycle() call with no version guard, it overrides zero stage timers from schema-14+ saves on the first simulation step, making the migration guard in save.rs partially dead code for the runtime path. This should be guarded or removed."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-f0846ba3","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: The helper at line 70 constructs replacement water from WaterState::default_for_volume_l(1.0), which sets DIC=20.0, DO=8.0, alkalinity=1.5, DOC=0.0, DON=0.0. The 50% water change mixes all of these into the tank, changing multiple chemistry parameters beyond chloride and sodium. The assertion compares pre-treatment vs post-treatment mortality within the same evolving run rather than against a matched control. Since improved DO, reduced organics, and alkalinity changes independently affect shrimp condition and mortality via the update_condition() pathway, the test cannot isolate whether chloride protection specifically reduced mortality. A parallel control tank or chemistry-matched water change that differs only in chloride/sodium is needed."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"71b0ccc2-5d9c-4f62-9f69-3e0b99156bf4"}
